6. Build & Execution Guide

6.1 Running the Monolithic Rust Backend

Ensure Bluetooth is turned on in your operating system settings.

Navigate to the backend folder and compile/run the single-binary monolith:

cd backend
cargo run --release


Verify the server starts on http://127.0.0.1:8080 and begins scanning for BLE peripherals.

6.2 Running the Modular Angular Frontend

Open a new terminal window and navigate to the frontend directory:

cd frontend
npm install
npx ng serve --open


Open http://localhost:4200 in your browser:

Connection Requests (/connections): View discovered peripherals, inspect RSSI proximity, and initiate or terminate GATT connection requests.

Packet Stream (/packets): Monitor live advertising (ADV_IND) and connection handshake packets with hex payload inspection and filtering.